	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(82.0, 358.0, 150.0, 144.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Drops name + host name (causes encoding-based errors)
Also sets ID as meta</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(292.0, 157.0, 476.0, 100.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">This procressing chain first discretizes to 10 equal bins (roughly 10th percentiles), then only selecting the highest bin (&gt;= 90th percentile) and then getting the ID column to query the original dataset</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/plain" rect="(837.3333333333333, 522.3333333333333, 258.0, 100.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Retrieving by index the properties with the top 10% of reviews</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/plain" rect="(957.0000000000002, 209.33333333333337, 167.0, 56.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Histogram by region (bonus!)</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/plain" rect="(1165.6666666666665, 522.6666666666666, 237.0, 75.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Returning count of properties in Chch city (343 as of current count)</text>
	</annotations>
